RNN-KRON: fix for #11
https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/11

In RTRL the term delta_kj*u_l sits inside the sum over the fed-back nodes, so it is added
nodes_1 times, raising the effective learning rate. Divide it by nodes_1 (same as adding it once).
In effect this only rescales the learning rate: the recursion is linear, so the fix is the same as
dividing eta by nodes_1 (see results/RNN_ISOLATION.md). Re-tune eta with it.

Applies to the sources prepared by src/tools/prepare.py (wrapped lines rejoined,
names lower-cased), not to src/borland/ directly:
  patch -p1 -d <prep dir> < src/fixes/RNN-KRON.patch

--- a/rnn.c
+++ b/rnn.c
@@ -165,7 +165,9 @@
 
         ann.layer_1[k].weights[l].sensitivity[j].sum += (ann.layer_1[j].weights[i].weight *
 ann.layer_1[k].weights[l].sensitivity[i-ann.nodes_0-1].sense +
+/* Fix #11: the training-rule term counted too many times
+ * https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/11 */
-KRONECKER(k,j)*ann.layer_0[l].output);
+KRONECKER(k,j)*ann.layer_0[l].output/ann.nodes_1);
                                                                         }
                                                                 }
                                                         }
